        "title": "fix(ci): stabilize the dead-export ratchet",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe enforced dead-export ratchet could change after a build because root `dist/**` output still participated in Knip issue analysis. The first merge also exposed ten current-main findings that were internal types, test-only helpers, or redundant re-exports rather than deletable code.\n\nRelated: #105575\nFollow-up to: #105826\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\n- Exclude root `dist/**` from both unused-file and issue analysis.\n- Keep internal-only types private.\n- Move test-only OpenAI transport helpers behind the existing `testing` facade.\n- Remove only the corresponding entries from the ratchet baseline.\n- Assert the root build-output exclusion in the guard test.\n\n## User Impact\n\nThe dead-export check now gives the same result before and after a full build. This is internal CI maintenance with no runtime or public protocol behavior change.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Blacksmith Testbox `tbx_01kxcrd053qn0rkkga48shv69k`, Actions run `29221822185`\n- `pnpm test test/scripts/check-deadcode-exports.test.ts src/agents/openai-tool-projection.live.test.ts src/agents/openai-transport-stream.test.ts src/agents/schema-normalization-runtime-contract.test.ts` — 343 tests passed\n- `pnpm deadcode:exports` — matched 5,512 entries before the build\n- `pnpm build` — passed; public plugin SDK declaration graph 5,089,173 / 5,200,000 bytes\n- `pnpm deadcode:exports` after `pnpm build` — matched the same 5,512 entries\n- `oxfmt --check` on all touched files — passed\n- Fresh `gpt-5.6-sol` autoreview — no accepted/actionable findings, 0.93 confidence\n\nAI-assisted: implementation and review used Codex; all listed proof ran against the branch tree on Blacksmith Testbox.\n",
